Anatomy Mirror derived meshes
Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 2.1 Japan (CC BY-SA 2.1 JP)

The skull, brain, eyes, skin, hand bones, and head muscles in anatomy.glb are
adapted from BodyParts3D / Anatomography, copyright Database Center for Life
Science (DBCLS). BodyParts3D is licensed under CC BY-SA 2.1 Japan:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.1/jp/deed.en

You may copy, share, and adapt these meshes provided you give credit, link the
licence, and distribute adaptations under the same licence.

The muscle layer is the 23 element meshes under FMA9616 in the BodyParts3D 4.0
isa tree (extraocular muscles, tongue, and palate), rigidly aligned to the 4.3
skull and released under the same licence. The muscles of facial expression are
not in that release.

The canonical face coordinates used only to align the meshes come from the
MediaPipe canonical face model (Apache License 2.0).
